{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>all, in achor</b> — like נסעו אחור, and it is a noun, or an adjective, or a [proper] name, and this is the correct one for the discerning." "<b>and achor</b> — a hint to the heart, for it is behind the going forth of the lips; and likewise יכחידנה תחת לשונו is a hint to the heart, for it is beneath the tongue." "<b>יְשַׁבְּחֶנָּה</b> — from ישביח שאון, meaning he silences. That is: כל רוח דעתו יוציא כסיל — the fool gives out the entirety of his mind's spirit and makes it known to others, as in ובקרב כסילים תודע; but the wise man, בלב — in the heart, which is behind what goes forth — ישבחו רוח דעתו, he silences his mind's spirit and does not make it known, as in בלב נבון תנוח חכמה."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:25.249777676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}